# Which plugin ref an older Discourse core should check out.
# Cores that match nothing here track the latest release, which targets the
# core pinned in .github/workflows/discourse-plugin.yml.
#
# Only refs CI has actually built are listed. The release job is gated on
# `needs: ci`, so a version tag exists only if the build it was cut from passed.

# Last release cut while CI built against core v2026.5.0.
# Capped below 2026.5.2: that patch backported the subcategory-count security
# fix (discourse/discourse@827f20a1), which v0.14.1 crashes on because it
# builds ProjectSerializer without a scope. Those cores need a later release.
<= 2026.5.1: v0.14.1

# Last release cut while CI built against core v3.5.2. CI moved to v2026.5.0
# before v0.11.0, so v0.10.1 is the newest ref proven on the 3.x line.
<= 3.5.2: v0.10.1
